#Robot Interface
I do not believe a digital interface is needed. It'd be more realistic to use simple switches that change its functionality. Think of a Bop It. 

From what we've discussed so far, we'll have both a seeker and a hider mode for the robot.

We just need a button to turn it on and off

To monitor the sensor and movement data: We can have it write to a few csv files.
They would include a timestamp, as well as the relevant data. If we want it to be on the physical robot and extracted off of it, we'd need to have something to store the data on, such as an SSD card. If it is connected to the internet or bluetooth, then we can send it directly to our device.

Note: The hider and seeker mode will be determined via spoken prompt, not button.
